"""PROPOSAL ONLY -- not committed as an active migration, not applied anywhere.
Kept as .draft so Alembic never auto-loads it; rename to .py and get sign-off,
then re-verify in an isolated database, before activation.

Chain position changed again this round: a fourth proposal,
0010_service_interactions.py.draft, has been inserted between 0009 and this
file. This file's `down_revision` is updated from "0009_fieldtest_participants"
to "0010_service_interactions" so the single intended linear chain is now
0006 -> 0007 -> 0009 -> 0010 -> 0008, with no new Alembic heads. 0008 and
0010 have no DB-content dependency on each other -- this is purely
chain-ordering, same as the 0007/0009 reordering in an earlier round. If
0010 is activated first (as proposed for this P0 fix) while this file stays
a .draft, nothing here needs to change again until 0008 itself is activated.

Schema fixed this round: the already-committed app/api/jiaan_webpush_routes.py
and app/services/jiaan_webpush.py (commit 0a3d16a) insert/lookup/ON CONFLICT
against an `endpoint_hash` column on jiaan_webpush_subscriptions that this
draft's CREATE TABLE never declared, and ON CONFLICT (endpoint_hash) has no
matching UNIQUE constraint to target -- applying the old draft as-is would
make `subscribe()` fail at runtime with "no unique or exclusion constraint
matching the ON CONFLICT specification" (or "column endpoint_hash does not
exist"). Also, `endpoint` is stored encrypted (Fernet, non-deterministic per
call) by the committed code, so UNIQUE on the ciphertext column was never
meaningful; uniqueness must live on the deterministic HMAC `endpoint_hash`
instead. Both are fixed in the DDL below. See
tests/test_jiaan_webpush_migration_consistency_unit.py for the static check
that keeps this draft in sync with the committed call sites going forward.

Outbox extension folded in this round: read-only inspection of both
ltc_pytest and the Staging database (ltc_v7_staging_20261114_195946) found
jiaan_webpush_deliveries already carries five extra columns (job_id,
expires_at, provider_accepted_at, app_opened_at, last_error_class) plus a
job_id FK to jobs(id), a partial unique index on job_id, a due-queue index,
and a NOT VALID expiry CHECK -- applied by hand from
run/integration_outbox_final_review_20261114_170707/REVIEWED_OUTBOX_SCHEMA.sql
(see that review's MIGRATION_REVIEW.md for the design rationale: reuses
`jobs` for idempotency/lease/attempts instead of a third outbox table).
That hand-applied SQL was never folded into this migration file, so a fresh
database built only from the committed Alembic chain would get the
*original*, narrower jiaan_webpush_deliveries shape -- missing columns real
dispatch code (app/services/jiaan_emergency_outbox.py) already reads and
writes. upgrade() below now applies the identical ADD COLUMN IF NOT
EXISTS / backfill / constraint / index steps as that reviewed SQL, inside
this same migration, so one `alembic upgrade head` on a brand-new database
reproduces exactly what ltc_pytest and Staging already have. Verified this
round on a from-scratch synthetic database (create -> upgrade head ->
confirm columns/indexes/constraints match -> drop database) and confirmed
idempotent against an already-extended database (IF NOT EXISTS / IF NOT
EXISTS guards throughout) by re-running upgrade against ltc_pytest, which
already had the extension, with zero errors and zero duplicate objects.

Fully additive for a fresh install (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS / CREATE
INDEX IF NOT EXISTS). The outbox extension adds columns to an
already-committed-as-new-by-this-same-migration table via ADD COLUMN IF NOT
EXISTS, so it is additive in the same sense 0010's tables are -- never
touches any table this migration did not itself just create. No pre-existing
data is deleted; the conservative expires_at backfill for legacy rows
mirrors the reviewed SQL exactly.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS safety gap fixed this round: if a table with
either name already exists -- most plausibly from someone having manually
run the older, buggy deploy/fieldtest/jiaan_webpush_schema.sql (the
"successful one-device test" referenced in app/services/jiaan_webpush.py,
which this session could not confirm or rule out without a database
connection) -- IF NOT EXISTS silently does nothing, leaving that old,
incomplete structure in place while Alembic still records this revision as
applied. upgrade() now re-reads each table's actual columns and unique
constraints after the CREATE statements and raises immediately if they
don't match what the committed application code requires. It never DROPs,
ALTERs, or overwrites anything by itself -- a mismatch stops the migration
with a message telling a human what to check.
"""
from alembic import op
import sqlalchemy as sa


def _columns(conn, table: str) -> set[str]:
    return {row[0] for row in conn.execute(sa.text(
        "SELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = :t"
    ), {"t": table})}


def _constraint_columns(conn, table: str, constraint_type: str) -> list[set[str]]:
    """每個符合 constraint_type 的限制各自涵蓋哪些欄位（可能有多個同類限制）。"""
    rows = conn.execute(sa.text(
        "SELECT tc.constraint_name, ccu.column_name "
        "FROM information_schema.table_constraints tc "
        "JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage ccu "
        "  ON tc.constraint_name = ccu.constraint_name AND tc.table_schema = ccu.table_schema "
        "WHERE tc.table_name = :t AND tc.constraint_type = :ct"
    ), {"t": table, "ct": constraint_type}).all()
    grouped: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
    for name, col in rows:
        grouped.setdefault(name, set()).add(col)
    return list(grouped.values())


def _verify_or_fail(conn, table: str, required_columns: set[str], required_unique: set[str]) -> None:
    existing = _columns(conn, table)
    if not existing:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{table} 建立後仍查無任何欄位，資料庫狀態異常，拒絕繼續，請人工檢查")
    missing = required_columns - existing
    if missing:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"{table} 已存在但缺少欄位：{sorted(missing)}；"
            "可能是不完整的舊版結構被 CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS 略過建立。"
            "本程式拒絕自動 DROP／ALTER／覆寫既有資料；"
            f"請人工確認 {table} 目前實際結構，視需要備份後手動補齊欄位，"
            "再重新套用此 Migration。"
        )
    if required_unique not in _constraint_columns(conn, table, "UNIQUE"):
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"{table} 缺少涵蓋 {sorted(required_unique)} 的 UNIQUE 限制；"
            "可能是舊版結構遺留。本程式拒絕自動修改限制，請人工確認後處理。"
        )


revision = "0008_jiaan_webpush"
down_revision = "0010_service_interactions"
branch_labels = None
depends_on = None


def upgrade() -> None:
    op.execute("""
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jiaan_webpush_subscriptions (
            id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
            user_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
            org_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
            endpoint text NOT NULL,
            endpoint_hash text NOT NULL UNIQUE,
            p256dh text NOT NULL,
            auth text NOT NULL,
            is_active boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
            created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
            updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
        )
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_jiaan_webpush_subs_org
            ON jiaan_webpush_subscriptions(org_id, is_active)
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jiaan_webpush_deliveries (
            id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
            emergency_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES jiaan1030_emergencies(id),
            subscription_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES jiaan_webpush_subscriptions(id),
            stage text NOT NULL CHECK (stage IN ('new','unacknowledged_60s','unacknowledged_180s')),
            status text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued',
            attempts int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
            created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
            attempted_at timestamptz,
            UNIQUE (emergency_id, subscription_id, stage)
        )
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_jiaan_webpush_delivery_q
            ON jiaan_webpush_deliveries(status, created_at)
    """)

    # Outbox extension (see docstring): reproduces
    # run/integration_outbox_final_review_20261114_170707/REVIEWED_OUTBOX_SCHEMA.sql
    # exactly, folded into this migration instead of staying a separate,
    # never-committed hand-applied script.
    op.execute("""
        ALTER TABLE jiaan_webpush_deliveries
          ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS job_id uuid,
          ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS expires_at timestamptz,
          ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS provider_accepted_at timestamptz,
          ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS app_opened_at timestamptz,
          ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS last_error_class text
    """)
    op.execute("""
        UPDATE jiaan_webpush_deliveries
        SET expires_at = created_at + interval '5 minutes'
        WHERE expires_at IS NULL
    """)
    op.execute("ALTER TABLE jiaan_webpush_deliveries ALTER COLUMN expires_at SET NOT NULL")
    op.execute("""
        DO $$
        BEGIN
            IF NOT EXISTS (
                SELECT 1 FROM pg_constraint
                WHERE conrelid = 'jiaan_webpush_deliveries'::regclass
                  AND conname = 'fk_jiaan_webpush_delivery_job'
            ) THEN
                ALTER TABLE jiaan_webpush_deliveries
                  ADD CONSTRAINT fk_jiaan_webpush_delivery_job
                  FOREIGN KEY (job_id) REFERENCES jobs(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT;
            END IF;
            IF NOT EXISTS (
                SELECT 1 FROM pg_constraint
                WHERE conrelid = 'jiaan_webpush_deliveries'::regclass
                  AND conname = 'ck_jiaan_webpush_expiry_after_create'
            ) THEN
                ALTER TABLE jiaan_webpush_deliveries
                  ADD CONSTRAINT ck_jiaan_webpush_expiry_after_create
                  CHECK (expires_at > created_at) NOT VALID;
            END IF;
        END $$;
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ux_jiaan_webpush_delivery_job
            ON jiaan_webpush_deliveries(job_id) WHERE job_id IS NOT NULL
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_jiaan_webpush_delivery_due
            ON jiaan_webpush_deliveries(status, expires_at, created_at)
            WHERE status IN ('queued', 'failed')
    """)

    conn = op.get_bind()
    _verify_or_fail(
        conn, "jiaan_webpush_subscriptions",
        {"id", "user_id", "org_id", "endpoint", "endpoint_hash", "p256dh", "auth",
         "is_active", "created_at", "updated_at"},
        {"endpoint_hash"},
    )
    _verify_or_fail(
        conn, "jiaan_webpush_deliveries",
        {"id", "emergency_id", "subscription_id", "stage", "status", "attempts",
         "created_at", "attempted_at", "job_id", "expires_at", "provider_accepted_at",
         "app_opened_at", "last_error_class"},
        {"emergency_id", "subscription_id", "stage"},
    )


def downgrade() -> None:
    # Intended for genuinely new tables this migration created. If either
    # table turns out to pre-date this migration (see the "one-device test"
    # note above) this would still delete it; a human must confirm that is
    # actually wanted (and that nothing else depends on the existing data)
    # before running this -- never run downgrade() unattended. Dropping
    # jiaan_webpush_deliveries also discards any job_id/provider_accepted_at/
    # app_opened_at/last_error_class history recorded by the outbox
    # extension -- exactly the data-loss risk the reviewed SQL's own
    # rollback outline already flagged as "not authorized, must not
    # auto-run"; this downgrade() must only be run with that understood.
    op.drop_table("jiaan_webpush_deliveries")
    op.drop_table("jiaan_webpush_subscriptions")
